id: core/source-bound-mental-model
title: "source-bound mental model and recursive cognitive passage"
kind: protocol-grammar
status: working-draft-0.1
updated: 2026-09-01

purpose: >
  Define how a Yawnbot may preserve an attributed source, compile correctable
  cognitive proposals, maintain a relationship to a subject, provision that
  model into an interaction, learn from consequences, and remain portable
  without turning generated interpretation, human judgment, interface state,
  or runtime agency into truth or authority.

one_model_rule: >
  This contract specializes the shared YAWN ontology. It does not create a
  second personal ontology, another master loop, a universal psychology, or a
  canonical claim that every thought must pass through the same stages.

foundational_distinction:
  yawnbot: >
    A persistent, addressable mental-model steward for one relationship to a
    subject. It can retain sources, questions, attributed positions,
    expression provisions, candidate moves, consequences, evaluations, proof,
    revisions, and relations. It is not identical to any one answer,
    expression, character, model provider, or rendered page.
  relationship: >
    Structurally first. The Yawnbot exists because an Agent or principal is in
    a consequential informational relationship with a subject, Arena, other
    Agent, project, question, artifact, or event.
  source: >
    What became available and from where. Exact source material remains
    distinguishable from every segmentation, summary, label, inference, and
    proposed model compiled from it.

substrate:
  form: typed-directed-graph
  rule: >
    Questions, positions, provisions, projections, moves, consequences,
    evaluations, proof adjudications, updates, cognitive facets, characters,
    and sources are addressable records joined by attributed typed relations.
    Any record may become the subject of a later question without changing its
    original type or forcing a single linear history.

human_facing_default_passage:
  status: noncanonical-rebuildable-view
  order:
    - question
    - position
    - expression_provision
    - projection
    - move
    - consequence
    - evaluation
    - proof_adjudication
    - update
    - reopened_or_new_question
  reading: >
    Question -> Position -> Expression provision -> Projection -> Move ->
    Consequence -> Evaluation -> Proof -> Update -> Question'.
  boundary: >
    This is a useful traversal through the graph, not the ontology itself.
    Stages may be absent, repeated, nested, disputed, simultaneous, or
    deliberately held. A Yawnbot may remain at inquiry, presence, waiting, or
    non-participation without failure.

terms:
  question: >
    What the Yawnbot or a participant is presently trying to resolve. A
    governing question can organize attention without becoming a terminal goal
    or requiring immediate closure.
  position:
    human_alias: answer
    definition: >
      An attributed, time-indexed stance offered in relation to a question.
      It carries sources, epistemic status, confidence, alternatives, revision,
      and acceptance state. An answer is never cast directly to truth.
  expression_provision: >
    A bounded configuration for making selected parts of a model available in
    an interaction: audience, purpose, medium, aperture, constraints, allowed
    projection kinds, and governing sources. It is a possibility for
    expression, not expression that has occurred.
  projection: >
    What an attributed Agent actually represents, proposes, commits, or
    attempts into an Arena under an expression provision. A draft projection
    is still distinct from an expressed projection and from its consequence.
  move: >
    A bounded attempted transition. A proposed or selected move is not chosen,
    authorized, executed, successful, or proved merely because it appears in a
    coherent model.
  consequence: >
    A source-backed change, response, trace, or observed delta following an
    executed move or other event in the Arena. Expected consequences belong to
    move selection; they are not consequence records.
  evaluation:
    human_alias: judgment
    definition: >
      An attributed assessment of a target against an explicit criteria
      snapshot. It records who evaluated what, in which relationship and Arena,
      using which criteria, observations, sources, rationale, uncertainty, and
      time. Conflicting evaluations may coexist.
    boundary: >
      Evaluation is not reality, consequence, moral authority, empirical
      proof, rightful choice, or permission to update canonical state.
  proof_adjudication: >
    A contract-facing determination of whether named evidence satisfies,
    fails, partially meets, contests, or remains insufficient for a previously
    stated proof condition. Evaluation can inform inquiry but cannot substitute
    for this adjudication.
  update: >
    An attributed revision proposal or authorized state change that identifies
    what changed, why, which proof and authority support it, what remains open,
    and which prior revision it supersedes.

source_compilation:
  passage:
    - preserve or reference the source with provenance and visibility
    - segment candidate thoughts without deleting the original context
    - propose questions, positions, criteria, relations, and cognitive facets
    - show source spans, confidence, alternatives, and unknowns
    - let the rightful participant confirm, reject, correct, add, defer, or inspect
    - promote only through an explicit attributed disposition event
  rule: >
    A compiler proposal remains a proposal even when fluent, high-confidence,
    repeated, emotionally resonant, or accepted as useful. Acceptance records
    authorship of a representation; it does not prove the represented claim.

cognitive_facets:
  examples:
    - thought
    - belief
    - goal
    - value
    - need
    - assumption
    - bias
    - boundary
    - habit
    - emotion
    - void
    - argument
    - quote
    - lacuna
  ontology_role: proposal-facet
  rule: >
    These are useful, revisable interpretive handles rather than claims that
    folk-psychological labels expose a person's hidden essence. Each facet
    remains source-bound, attributed, confidence-labeled, and separately
    ratified before durable use.

character_view:
  definition: >
    An optional symbolic, spatial, narrative, or game representation of one or
    more model records. Nestheads characters may make cognition inspectable and
    memorable without becoming the source of truth.
  agent_boundary: >
    A character View is not an Agent. Promote a candidate to Agent only through
    the existing identity, persistence, capability, memory, relationship,
    authority, activation, stop, and retirement contracts.

selection_and_learning:
  before_a_move: >
    Inquiry and move selection compare predicted fit, expected consequences,
    gates, reversibility, information value, cost, affected relationships, and
    proofability using the orientation available at that time.
  after_a_move: >
    Consequences are observed first. Evaluations then assess targets against
    explicit criteria. Proof adjudicates named tests. Authorized updates revise
    the model without rewriting the historical selection receipt or pretending
    later knowledge was available earlier.
  recursion: >
    An evaluation may open "Why was this judged this way?" That question can
    expose criteria, values, assumptions, histories, relationships, and
    conflicting perspectives. The recursive opening creates new graph paths;
    it does not erase the evaluated record.

expression_and_access:
  portable_package: >
    A Yawnbot package may carry stable IDs, bounded snapshots, source refs,
    relation edges, expression provisions, audience policies, revisions, and
    integrity information so another intelligence can orient without inheriting
    the principal's identity, beliefs, agreement, consent, privacy, authority,
    or proof.
  connection: >
    Connecting one Yawnbot to another creates an attributed relationship edge
    with scope and revocation. It does not merge identities, silently import
    truth, or widen either side's visibility or authority.
  exposure_requirement: >
    A record may propose that particular information should be exposed to a
    network or audience. That requirement remains intent until owners,
    affected principals, audience, consent, redaction, and publication
    authorization are explicit.

runtime_binding:
  rule: >
    The mental model and a runtime Yawnbot Agent remain distinct. A source-bound
    model may exist without any active Agent. Candidate, sleeping, active, and
    retired bindings follow the Objective Holon, Agency Holarchy, and execution
    authority contracts.
  provider_boundary: >
    A model provider or connected intelligence is not the Yawnbot's identity,
    rightful principal, decision owner, or authority source.

illegal_casts:
  - "source -> interpretation"
  - "segmentation -> thought truth"
  - "compiler proposal -> accepted cognition"
  - "facet label -> identity"
  - "question -> obligation to answer"
  - "position or answer -> truth"
  - "expression provision -> projection"
  - "draft projection -> expression event"
  - "projection -> move"
  - "move proposal -> choice"
  - "choice -> authorization"
  - "execution -> consequence"
  - "expected consequence -> observed consequence"
  - "consequence -> evaluation"
  - "evaluation or judgment -> proof"
  - "proof -> authorization or update"
  - "publication intent -> publication"
  - "connection -> inheritance"
  - "character View -> Agent"
  - "default traversal View -> ontology"

conformance:
  aggregate_schema: schemas/source-bound-yawnbot.v0.1.schema.json
  evaluation_schema: schemas/evaluation-record.v0.1.schema.json
  fixture: fixtures/dave-kickstarter-nestheads.source-bound-yawnbot.v0.1.json
  validator: scripts/validate-source-bound-yawnbot-v0.1.mjs
  tests: tests/source-bound-yawnbot-v0.1.test.mjs

first_dogfood:
  coordinate: dave/kickstarter/nestheads
  purpose: >
    Demonstrate a founder's source-preserving relationship to an unfinished
    public commitment without publishing private source text, inventing
    consequences, treating context as absolution, claiming the draft was sent,
    or claiming the proposed mental-model interface fulfills the original
    campaign promise.
  current_boundary:
    - source references only; private exact text is not embedded
    - founder update remains a draft projection
    - send remains a proposed move
    - no message consequence exists before execution
    - no proof or canonical update is claimed
    - public access remains an unauthorized candidate policy

related_contracts:
  - core/orientation.yawn
  - core/co-orientation-loop.yawn
  - core/inquiry-selection.yawn
  - core/move-selection.yawn
  - core/projection-and-aperture.yawn
  - core/proof-and-boundary.yawn
  - core/choice-and-move-selection.yawn
  - core/objective-holon.yawn
  - schemas/agency-holarchy.v0.2.schema.json
  - schemas/objective-holon.v0.1.schema.json
  - interface/new-yawn-coordinate-resolution-v0.1.yawn

open_lacunae:
  - whether Position should receive a stable v1 contract outside this aggregate
  - how exact source spans are encrypted, revoked, and selectively disclosed
  - how multi-principal evaluation and publication conflicts are negotiated
  - how portable packages bind integrity without freezing living models
  - how model usefulness, burden, and agency effects should be compared against simpler notes
  - how a private Dave record becomes a sanitized public Kickstarter View through explicit receipts

proof:
  success: >
    A fresh intelligence can distinguish source, inference, attributed stance,
    provision, actual expression, move state, consequence, evaluation, proof,
    update, audience authority, character View, and runtime Agent while tracing
    each record to sources and preserving unresolved questions.
  falsifier: >
    A simpler source-linked note system performs equally or better on
    attribution, correction, privacy, question quality, coordination, movement,
    proof closure, retained agency, and cognitive burden—or this grammar causes
    false psychological certainty, compulsive modeling, identity reification,
    surveillance pressure, or publication without consent.
